From d71ead8b9c1f3de69a66a909fa6cc51398e87137 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claudius <claudiusthebot@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:00:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: add an UNTESTED minimal MAX77705 port driver

Reports attach, power and data role and orientation from the CCIC
firmware, and follows them with the USB role switch, the orientation
switch and VBUS. Off by default: TYPEC_MAX77705 is not set in the config,
and only the new -typec test DTB has the node.

No PD requests and no firmware update path: the opcode allowlist holds
0x06, 0x54 and 0x55 with one permitted payload each, and the regmap can
only write masks and a one-byte mailbox. Never run on hardware.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/Makefile             |   1 +
 .../qcom/sm8250-samsung-gts7xlwifi-typec.dts  | 102 ++++
 drivers/usb/typec/Kconfig                     |  15 +
 drivers/usb/typec/Makefile                    |   1 +
 drivers/usb/typec/max77705_typec.c            | 505 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 624 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-samsung-gts7xlwifi-typec.dts
 create mode 100644 drivers/usb/typec/max77705_typec.c

